\subtree{
\title{3.3 Random exports (\code{\verb~|work/s2/gen/fuzz.py~}, seeds 11 - 14, \code{\verb~|work/s2/attacks/fuzz/~}, 498 exports)}

\p{One random constant per export - an axiom (125 exports), a definition with hint regular (151) / abbrev (56) / opaque (63), or the constructor of a random structure (103) - over a random telescope of 2 to 8 positions drawn from: a sort \code{\verb~|Sort u_k~} (level parameters shared or not), an element of an earlier sort (a proof when that sort is instantiated at 0, a Nat or Bool at 1), a Nat, a proof of \code{\verb~|Q n~} for an earlier Nat, a proposition, a proof of an earlier proposition, a proof of \code{\verb~|True~}, a member of an axiom family \code{\verb~|Fam n~}, a function, a proof of a Pi into Prop. A definition's body reads a random subset through axioms into Nat, each read wrapped at random in a let, a beta redex, an inner lambda or a \code{\verb~|Nat.rec~}. Each export makes 4 to 12 TRUE claims (the sides differ in proofs, in the representation of equal data, and in unread parameters, at several level vectors); a \code{\verb~|-bad~} export ends with one FALSE claim that changes the value of one data position that matters. The official verdict was the predicted one for all 498.}

\table{
\tr{\th{}\th{exports}\th{\code{\verb~|v0~}}\th{\code{\verb~|skip~}}\th{\code{\verb~|both~}}\th{\code{\verb~|skip0~}}\th{official}}
