\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|-true~}}\td{136}\td{136 A}\td{136 A}\td{136 A}\td{136 A}\td{136 accept}}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{3.4 Do the attacks have teeth? Seeded faults (\code{\verb~|work/s2/mcopy/~}, \code{\verb~|work/s2/dist3~}, \code{\verb~|-Ds2.bug=N~})}

\p{A private copy of the module with one fault at a time, \code{\verb~|skip~} configuration, on the \code{\verb~|-bad~} exports of 3.1, of half of 3.3 and of package S's \code{\verb~|facts-*~} / \code{\verb~|mask-*~} (301 exports: 96 + 183 + 22). "Caught" = at least one false claim is ACCEPTED by the faulty build (so the suite would have shown the fault).}

\table{
\tr{\th{Fault}\th{What is broken}\th{False claims ACCEPTED that the unmodified build rejects}\th{Caught by}}
\tr{\td{1}\td{\code{\verb~|propMask~}: a manifest sort that MAY be zero (a level parameter) counts as a proposition}\td{8}\td{\code{\verb~|lvl-*-generic-bad~}, \code{\verb~|-renamed-bad~} (8). The random exports cannot catch it: their claims are closed}}
\tr{\td{5}\td{\code{\verb~|propMask~} shifted by one position}\td{41}\td{fuzz 35, \code{\verb~|etas~} 2, S's \code{\verb~|facts~} 2 and \code{\verb~|mask~} 1, \code{\verb~|prop~} 1}}
\tr{\td{2}\td{\code{\verb~|unreadMask~} shifted by one position}\td{18}\td{\code{\verb~|unread~} 11, fuzz 6, S's \code{\verb~|facts~} 1}}
\tr{\td{7}\td{de Bruijn arithmetic of the unread mask off by one (\code{\verb~|binders(mask, lam + 1)~})}\td{40}\td{\code{\verb~|unread~} 21, fuzz 13, \code{\verb~|prop~} 3, S's \code{\verb~|facts~} 3}}
\tr{\td{4}\td{ETAS mask indexed by the field number instead of \code{\verb~|nparams + field~}}\td{2}\td{\code{\verb~|etas-param-proof-bad~}, one random structure}}
\tr{\td{6}\td{the unread mask also under APP}\td{0}\td{no effect to catch: no head that reaches c8 has an unread mask (the one candidate, an \code{\verb~|opaque~} constant, has no value facts: \code{\verb~|facts.use.unreadSet~} stays 0)}}
\tr{\td{3}\td{the \code{\verb~|differ~} rule dropped (a proof position is skipped whatever its domain reads)}\td{0}\td{consistent with 2.2: I could not build a false claim from the absence of the rule, and none of the 301 is one}}
}

\p{So a mask that is wrong by a position, by a de Bruijn index or by a universe instantiation IS shown by the suite (\code{\verb~|work/s2/out/seeded-bug*.tsv~}, \code{\verb~|work/s2/seeded-summary.py~}); the suite is weakest on the ETAS index (2 exports).}
}

\subtree{
\title{3.5 What the options remove: a seeded fault of INFERENCE}

\p{Fault 10 of the private copy makes \code{\verb~|Infer.twD~} skip the comparison of an argument's type with its domain (an inference bug). \code{\verb~|ctx-wrong-proof-in-value-bad~} - statement \code{\verb~|f 1 (pf 1) = f 1 (pf 1)~}, value \code{\verb~|Eq.refl (f 1 (pf 2))~}, \code{\verb~|pf 2 : Q 2~} where \code{\verb~|Q 1~} is required - is then still REJECTED by v0, because the official comparison of the two proof arguments compares their types (\code{\verb~|Q 2~} against \code{\verb~|Q 1~}), and ACCEPTED under \code{\verb~|skip~} and \code{\verb~|both~}, which do not look at a proof position. With the options, conversion is no longer a second check of what inference let through.}
}

\subtree{
\title{3.6 Real corpora under \code{\verb~|shortcheck~} (\code{\verb~|work/s2/corpus-shortcheck.sh~}, \code{\verb~|both~}, one worker)}

\p{Every T that skipped a position (CARGS, ETAS) or came from B1 / B12 is re-derived at once by the complete official procedure with all switches off; a T that the complete procedure does not find is an audit failure (\code{\verb~|E_AUDIT~}, the unit is declined). A wrong mask would show here as soon as a comparison that the official procedure answers F is answered T (failed same-head comparisons of unequal data are frequent in these files).}

